<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ketevan the Martyr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1565–1624</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Saint Ketevan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ketevan, known as Saint Ketevan the Martyr, was a queen of Kakheti in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and the mother of King Teimuraz I. Sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> as a hostage, she was held for years at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> and, after refusing to give up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, was tortured to death on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> in 1624. Augustinian missionaries took relics of her to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a>, and she is venerated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgian-orthodox-church">Georgian Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ketevan-the-martyr.jpg" alt="Ketevan the Martyr" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This work is in the public domain in its country of origin and other countries a... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Ketevan,_Lisbon_fresco_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
